      {
        "id": 77696,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-22T18:42:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p>If Chutes and Ladders is a game, then flipping a coin is a game.</p></blockquote><p>Of course it's a game.&nbsp; If I want to flip a coin over and over to see how many heads in a row I get, that's a game.&nbsp; A game is anything you do for fun.&nbsp; If someone feels their games have to include a skill component to be fun, that's perfectly fine, but it doesn't invalidate every other kind of game in the world.</p>",
